# Revisions git blame should skip: bulk reformats with no behaviour change.
#
# Without this, `git blame` on the reformatted files answers "who ran the
# formatter" instead of "who wrote this line" — which is the question that
# actually matters when the person who wrote it graduated two years ago.
#
# GitHub honours this file automatically in its blame view. For local git, opt
# in once per clone:
#
#     git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# Only add commits that are provably formatting-only. One SHA per line, with a
# comment naming it.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HEADS UP: PRs in this repo are SQUASH-merged, so a branch commit's SHA does
# not survive the merge — a pre-merge SHA listed here would silently match
# nothing. Each entry has to be the squashed commit as it lands on `staging`,
# which means adding it in a small follow-up commit after the merge.
